      "id": "reading",
      "className": "panel",
      "type": "rich",
      "html": "<span class=\"number\">INPUT · 4 MIN</span><h2>Read, listen to your own voice, and notice</h2><p class=\"instruction\">Read once for meaning. Then read aloud; on the second pass, notice how the speaker uses whole phrases.</p><div class=\"reading\">I'd recommend testing the new process with one small team. I think changing everything at once would be difficult. The main reason is that we don't know how much help people will need. For example, a small test lets us answer questions before the whole company starts. I agree that we want to move quickly. However, we also need time to learn. We decided to ask one team to try it for a week. After that, we can compare the results and choose the next step. What do you think would be most useful to measure during that week?</div>"
    },
